PARITY MAPPING  (web -> Apple platform tokens; no Tailwind ported, no raw hex)
  rows: ResourceRow[]            -> [ResourceRow]; per-row props in ResourceRowInputs (Equatable subset).
  percent -> severity ternary    -> ResourceSeverity.classify: nil->normal, >=90->critical, >=70->warn,
    (warn 70%, critical 90%)        else normal (verbatim port; thresholds are named constants).
  bar colour bg-{green|amber|red}-400 -> ResourceSeverity.barTone (shared TSTone): normal->success,
                                   warn->warning, critical->danger -> Color.TS.status* (theme-aware).
  text colour (normal->primary,  -> ResourceSeverity.valueColor: normal->Color.TS.textPrimary (NOT green),
    warn->amber, critical->red)     warn->warning, critical->danger. The normal split (green bar / primary
                                   text) is reproduced EXACTLY and unit-asserted.
  value (tabular-nums, medium)   -> Text(Font.TS.body,.medium,.monospacedDigit, valueColor).
  metaText (ml-1 text-xs muted)  -> Text(Font.TS.bodySm, Color.TS.textMuted); shown iff non-empty
                                   (web `{row.metaText && …}` — empty string is falsy -> dropped).
  label (flex-1 truncate)        -> Text(Font.TS.body, textSecondary), lineLimit(1).tail, maxWidth:.infinity.
  icon?: ReactNode               -> @ViewBuilder icon slot erased to AnyView?; decorative
                                   (accessibilityHidden), tinted Color.TS.textSecondary.
  bar h-1.5 track white/.06      -> ResourceUsageBar: Capsule track Color.TS.border + tinted fill; width =
    fill width=clamp(0..100)        clamp(percent,0,100) (web Math.max/min); height 6.
  transition-all duration-slow   -> bar fill width animates on TSAnimation.slow(reduceMotion:) — instant
                                   under Reduce Motion (a faithful reproduction of the web transition,
                                   chosen over the static TSMetricBar so the animation is preserved).
  role=progressbar aria-valuenow -> row is one a11y element: label + a11y value reads value, sub-label, and
    =Math.round(percent)            "<round(percent)>% used" (ResourcesPanelStrings.usageValue, localizable).
                                   aria-valuenow uses the UNCLAMPED round (web), width uses the clamp — split
                                   preserved + unit-asserted.
  <h3>Resources</h3>             -> Text(Font.TS.body,.semibold, textPrimary) + .isHeader; the one fixed web
                                   string, via ResourcesPanelStrings.title (P1/S10).
  footnote?: ReactNode           -> @ViewBuilder footnote slot erased to AnyView?, styled Font.TS.bodySm /
                                   textMuted (web mt-3 text-xs muted cascade).
  GlassPanel (p-4)               -> .padding(TSSpacing.lg) + .tsGlassPanel() (the repo GlassPanel peer).
  id / className                 -> id -> OptionalAccessibilityIdentifier (DOM-id peer for anchor + UI
                                   tests); className (Tailwind-merge affordance) has NO native equivalent —
                                   intentionally not ported (DISCLOSED).
  tokens                         -> TSSpacing/TSRadius/Color.TS/Font.TS/TSTone/TSAnimation — no Tailwind, no hex.

